Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F64%2Ff0%2F0adc6b7e4d569f8d03e0096fc60b%2Funtitled-1350936.jpg" class="img" alt="The destroyed location of the original Cafe 11/11 in Kherson, Ukraine. CREDIT: Svet Jacqueline for NPR UKRAINE" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 The destroyed location of the original Cafe 11/11 in Kherson, Ukraine.  CREDIT: Svet Jacqueline for NPR UKRAINE                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Svet Jacqueline for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;In Ukraine's Kherson region, a brief ceasefire brought a momentary return to normalcy. Brokered by first lady Melania Trump and Pope Leo last week, the truce allowed hundreds of residents to evacuate from a Russian-occupied town and provided a rare few days of peace in a frontline city. Russia and Ukraine agreed to the deal to help Oleshky, a town near Kherson that was occupied by Russian troops in 2022. The troops had mined the land around it, and food and medicine were rarely able to reach the people. This short pause in hostilities was a welcome relief, allowing families to fill the sidewalks, shoppers to hurry to stock up and cafe-goers to enjoy art-filled spaces. These photos &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/g-s1-151238/ukraine-russia-ceasefire-oleshky-kherson" target="_blank"&gt;capture a brief glimpse of everyday life&lt;/a&gt; for these people.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-151597" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3008;         --source-height: 1692;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+154/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb2%2F1c%2F4ffe7fad493ca73dd7ae0eddc972%2Fdsc-1009.JPG" class="img" alt="Election cake is a sweet civic tradition dating back to 1771. The annual Election Cake Bake-Off at Connecticut&amp;#039;s Old State House in Harford, CT, has continued the celebration for more than 250 years." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Election cake is a sweet civic tradition dating back to 1771. The annual Election Cake Bake-Off at Connecticut's Old State House in Harford, CT, has continued the celebration for more than 250 years.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Barbara Glassman Dell                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;At Connecticut's Old State House, the annual Election Cake Bake-Off has been celebrating the sweet civic tradition of election cake for more than 250 years. This &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6026494/election-cake-bake-off-hartford-connecticut" target="_blank"&gt;dessert has evolved&lt;/a&gt; from what it once was: a tough fruitcake, often soaked in alcohol.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Chemical manufacturer 3M has &lt;a href="https://www.publicradioeast.org/2026-11-04/3m-agrees-to-7-35-billion-settlement-in-nationwide-pfas-firefighting-foam-litigation" target="_blank"&gt;reached a $7.35 billion settlement&lt;/a&gt; to resolve thousands of personal injury claims related to toxic chemicals found in firefighting foam. (via &lt;a href="http://www.publicradioeast.org/" target="_blank"&gt;PRE News &amp; Ideas&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A new study shows that loon populations are declining across the birds' southern breeding range, but Maine stands out with a &lt;a href="https://www.mainepublic.org/climate/2026-11-03/loon-study-reveals-troubling-trends-but-maine-may-be-a-bright-spot" target="_blank"&gt;slight increase in loon productivity&lt;/a&gt;, according to Birds Canada. (via &lt;a href="https://www.mainepublic.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Maine Public&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
