mages-2302879767.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1024x683+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F8a%2F809c3c6446548b49d2de40521ae6%2Fgettyimages-2302879767.jpg" class="img" alt="A voter casts their ballot at a polling station during the midterm elections in Portland, Maine, on November 3." fetchpriority="high" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A voter casts their ballot at a polling station during the midterm elections in Portland, Maine, on November 3.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Angela Weiss/AFP via Getty Images/AFP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A version of this essay first appeared in the &lt;/em&gt;Up First&lt;em&gt; newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1180232252/up-first-newsletter" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Subscribe here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;em&gt;to get the news you need to start your day — plus a little fun — every weekday and Sunday.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;With the arrival of Election Day, months of campaign ads and rallies come to an abrupt halt. Big names, including President Trump and former President Barack Obama, have spent weeks on the road advocating for candidates in tight races.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;As Election Day approached, political prospects across the U.S. burned through their final reserves of stamina to get every vote they can. Experts have projected that the Senate and House will be won with razor-thin margins.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Throughout October, &lt;em&gt;Morning Edition&lt;/em&gt; has been on the road speaking to voters in &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/06/g-s1-146559/morning-edition-2026-midterms-election-voters-states" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;six pivotal states&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; that could decide which party controls Congress.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-6022233-100" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-6022233-100" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Leila Fadel reported from Maine. A Martínez made his way to the big state of Texas. Steve Inskeep went to North Carolina and Georgia. And Michel Martin traveled to Ohio and Michigan. The hosts traveled to these states with the goal of speaking with a variety of people across political lines about the issues that will inform their votes. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;In Maine, Fadel &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/06/nx-s1-5989427/maine-men-democrats-male-voters-midterms" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;got &lt;/u&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;u&gt;reel &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;u&gt;with men&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. She went fly fishing and discussed the Democratic Party's perceived "man problem." Trump won the 2024 election largely because most men across the country voted for him. The men Fadel spoke to varied in age and political affiliation, but they all agreed on two things: They loved to fish and they wanted change. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998165/texans-beef-prices-election-season" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Beef is king&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in Texas. And its rising price has affected the quality of life. Martínez spoke with residents, business owners and farmers about what's driving the price hikes and how it may sway their vote.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Inskeep did some door-knocking in and around Marietta, Ga., north of Atlanta. The railroad tracks that split the city also &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/20/nx-s1-6007258/georgia-midterms-2026-voters" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;split its residents across political lines&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Inskeep spoke with voters on both sides. Come election day, he'll see which side turned out in greater numbers.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;In Michigan, Trump made increasingly personal attacks against Democratic candidate for Senate Abdul El-Sayed, even calling him a "jihadist." Voters there told Martin that &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/27/nx-s1-6018541/michigan-voters-election-fatigue-campaign-rhetoric" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;they are burned out&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and frustrated with the political system. Martin also spoke with Michigan voters about the effects of tariffs on their businesses and everyday lives.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The voters in these states gave Fadel, Martínez, Inskeep and Martin an in-depth perspective on how the battle for the Senate and House majorities may shake out come Election Day. Below they share their biggest takeaways from their trips:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-6022233-101" class="bucketwrap statichtml"&gt;             &lt;blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DerTZbeiQB1/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;amp;utm_campaign=loading" data-instgrm-version="14" style=" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; width:-webkit-calc(100% - 2px); width:calc(100% - 2px);"&gt;&lt;div style="padding:16px;"&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DerTZbeiQB1/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;amp;utm_campaign=loading" style=" background:#FFFFFF; line-height:0; padding:0 0; text-align:center; text-decoration:none; width:100%;" target="_blank"&gt; &lt;div style=" display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center;"&gt; &lt;div style="background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 40px; margin-right: 14px; width: 40px;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-grow: 1; justify-content: center;"&gt; &lt;div style=" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; width: 100px;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style=" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; width: 60px;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding: 19% 0;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="display:block; height:50px; margin:0 auto 12px; width:50px;"&gt;&lt;svg width="50px" height="50px" viewbo