s://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7843x4412+0+294/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe0%2F8b%2F3aa3d12341a78636a49ef4c1af2d%2Fgettyimages-1210344576.jpg" class="img" alt="Getty Images" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Getty Images                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;"Your Turn" is a &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/series/g-s1-146135/your-turn-with-allison-aubrey" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;special series&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; from NPR's Allison Aubrey, exploring how to navigate your way through midlife.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Burnout can be a challenge during midlife. As work and home obligations take up more of your focus, burnout can slowly sap your sense of joy and wonder in everyday life. Psychiatrist Judith Joseph says there's a term for this: anhedonia. It's the inability or reduced capacity to experience pleasure from things that are normally enjoyable. Joseph says it can accompany what she calls "high-functioning depression," and she describes it as depression's "silent sister." Here's what the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/29/nx-s1-5996687/anhedonia-quiz-high-functioning-depression" target="_blank"&gt;research shows about high-functioning depression&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ Research published in the journal &lt;em&gt;Cureus&lt;/em&gt; confirmed the hypothesis that people with high-functioning depression have increased levels of anhedonia and trauma. Parents and caregivers had the highest high-functioning depression scores.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ High-functioning depression is not an official diagnosis in the DSM-5. People who keep functioning may not recognize their symptoms or seek treatment until they're burned out.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ Joseph has developed an &lt;a href="https://drjudithjoseph.com/anhedoniaquiz/?gf_page_4=1" target="_blank"&gt;anhedonia quiz&lt;/a&gt;. While it's not a diagnostic tool, it can be helpful to take stock of the obstacles preventing you from living a more joyful life.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ Joseph also developed a framework to combat anhedonia, called the Five V's: Validation, Venting, Values, Vision and Vitals.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Want to know more? &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/29/nx-s1-5996687/anhedonia-quiz-high-functioning-depression" target="_blank"&gt;Read more about the Five V's&lt;/a&gt;, sign up for the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/your-turn?utm_source=npr_newsletter&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=20261025&amp;utm_term=11023374&amp;utm_campaign=health&amp;utm_id=61181210&amp;orgid=554&amp;uniquet=DZkDymDM4pIAJJ9-xOF9QA&amp;utm_att1=" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your Turn&lt;/em&gt; newsletter&lt;/a&gt; and listen to the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/g-s1-143389/your-turn-with-allison-aubrey" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your Turn &lt;/em&gt;podcast&lt;/a&gt; for tools and inspiring stories that blend science and wisdom to help you move forward to what's next.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Behind the story&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;by &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/122805042/tamara-keith" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tamara Keith&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, senior political correspondent&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-img-6316533" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5259;         --source-height: 2958;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5259x2958+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2Fa2%2Fd8ba90f8446a9f4d0518ab9fbb2e%2Fd49676ad-eeef-4a9d-a717-770446586030.png" class="img" alt="" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 People arrive at a polling location during early voting in the midterm election, in Atlanta, Georgia, on October 13, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Photo by Erik S. Lesser/AFP via Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;At this stage in the midterms, all that's left is the voting and the waiting. On election night, I'll be in Studio 31 at NPR headquarters with browser tabs full of spreadsheets, watching the results roll in and sharing context with NPR listeners.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;One of those spreadsheets lists all the congressional districts that have been redrawn since 2024 as part of a mid-decade redistricting push by President Trump. Facing down the historical precedent that the president's party usually loses seats in the midterms, the president pressured Republican-led states to create more sure-thing GOP districts.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;But headed into voting, the results in two-thirds of those districts are very much up in the air. In some cases, Democrats are favored. These are places Trump would have won by 10 points just two years ago.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Last month, I saw that the president had a campaign rally scheduled in Greenville, N.C. But national Republicans essentially stopped running ads for Michael Whatley — Trump's handpicked nominee — and diverted resources to states with more competitive races. So, why was the president holding another rally? I reached out to a few sources in the state.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;What I learned is that the real reason for the president's trip was almost certainly to help the Republican candidate in eastern North Carolina's first congressional district. It is now one of the most hotly contested and expensive House races in the country, despite new district lines that should have made it an easy Republican pick-up.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Two days of driving through this very large district, one Trump rally, two bags of gummy candy and a lot of coffee later, I was back in the office digging into my spreadsheet of congressional districts. NC-01 isn't an isolated case. A majority of districts redrawn to be a firewall for a Republican majority have turned out to be far more competitive than expected.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;So, Tuesday night (and beyond), I'll be filling in the wins and losses to see how this gambit turned out. In the meantime, read more from me about &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/01/nx-s1-6022128/trump-rally-2026-midterms-republicans" target="_blank"&gt;how Trump is spending his final days&lt;/a&gt; on the campaign trail. And, you can listen to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/01/nx-s1-6023356/who-decides-the-future-of-america" target="_blank"&gt;everything you need to know&lt;/a&gt; about the midterms on &lt;em&gt;Up First: The Sunday Story&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-151168" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5666;         --source-height: 3187;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5666x3187+0+295/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F05%2F6e%2F8562f8374158a09f65515925a89e%2Fgettyimages-2236122542.jpg" class="img" alt="Sen. Chris Murphy, D-Conn., appears at a news conference at the U.S. Capitol on September 18, 2025. Murphy&amp;#039;s office says he was hospitalized this weekend with a stroke." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Sen. Chris Murphy, D-Conn., appears at a news conference at the U.S. Capitol on September 18, 2025. Murphy's office says he was hospitalized this weekend with a stroke.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images/Getty Images North America                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sen. Chris Murphy, D-Conn., 53, has been hospitalized after &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/01/nx-s1-6025467/chris-murphy-stroke" target="_blank"&gt;experiencing a stroke&lt;/a&gt;. His office reports that he is expected to make a full recovery.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Hackers &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/31/nx-s1-6024426/binance-crypto-heist-cyber-criminals-north-korea" target="_blank"&gt;stole more than $6 billion&lt;/a&gt; from Binance, the world's largest cryptocurrency exchange. The FBI concluded that North Korea carried out the attack.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Oil companies reported huge profits in the quarter that just ended. Together, ExxonMobil, Shell and Chevron &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/31/nx-s1-6008072/oil-company-profits-gasoline-diesel-prices" target="_blank"&gt;earned more than $36 billion&lt;/a&gt; as the war in Iran drives up gas prices.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
